# Every path in this repository requires review from the owner.
#
# Paired with branch protection's "require review from Code Owners", this makes
# the requirement specific rather than generic: a pull request needs *this*
# approval, not merely any collaborator's. Today that distinction is moot —
# there is one collaborator — but it is the setting that stays correct if that
# ever changes, and it is cheaper to establish now than to remember later.
#
# Note that GitHub does not let an author approve their own pull request, so
# the owner's own PRs are merged using the admin bypass rather than by
# self-approving. That is expected, not a misconfiguration.

